<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποδια-στολή</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slight stop,</i> between
			words in speaking or reading, <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				11.3.35
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>mark to divide words from one another</i> (most Greek writing
			being continuous), e. g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστιν,
			ἄξιος</span> to distinguish it from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστι Νάξιος,</span> Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>T.<i><span class="en">
				674
			</span></i>, Sch.D.T.<i><span class="en">
				p.24H.
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				701.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1465.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>slight change</i> in positions of the planets, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				73.17
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
